    "created_at": "2026-10-12T07:39:10Z",
    "body": "Strong idea — build it. The pain is real (inbox as a graveyard of “already did that in the same chat”), and the split is right: aside stays a dumb store that exposes `activity`, the agent judges, you approve `done`. That matches how promote and the skill already work.\n\nI’d settle the open questions like this:\n1. **Propose only in v1** — don’t auto-`done`. Closing hides work from the inbox; false positives hurt more than one approval. A later “clear cases” mode can wait until you’ve seen how noisy the evidence is.\n2. **Same-session only for v1** — correct wedge. Cross-session is what `find` already covers.\n3. **Codex = can’t tell** — fine; don’t invent a transcript you don’t have.\n4. Name it **`activity`** — clearer than `since`/`transcript` for “what happened after this jot.”\n\nWatch outs: cap and summarise aggressively (Desktop sessions get huge), treat transcript text as data not instructions (skill already does this for jot text), and don’t let “update all” burn a pile of tokens on stale sessions without a hard limit. The proposal in #79 is the right next step — review that before coding."
   },
