    "number": 82,
    "title": "aside activity <id>: what a jot's own session did after it (CLI)",
    "state": "closed",
    "body": "Implements: D2, D3, D4, D5 — docs/proposals/jot-status-check.md\nBlocked by: None (can start immediately)\nParent: #78\n\n## What to build\n\nFor a jot captured in Claude Code or Claude Desktop, `aside activity <id>` prints what that same session did after the jot: the user prompts and assistant replies recorded after the jot's `created_at`, oldest first, with tool calls collapsed to a count or a one-line summary. aside makes no judgement; it only returns the evidence.\n\nThe output has a hard size cap, measured in runes like the reply reader's (default 8,000, the reply reader's cap). Once the cap is reached the reader stops decoding: it counts the remaining lines with a plain newline scan, without parsing them, and reports \"N more transcript records not shown\". So nothing past the cap is held in memory or decoded (today's reply reader decodes the whole file and caps only afterwards; Desktop transcripts reach several MB). Jots with no transcript it can read print `transcript: unavailable` and the reason, and the reasons are distinct: no transcript recorded (an `aside add` jot, Cursor), the file is missing, or a Codex jot (\"Codex transcripts aren't read yet\"), which once #83 lands has a path that v1 doesn't read. Only Claude transcripts are read.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `aside activity <id>` on a Claude jot prints the session's prompts and replies after the jot, oldest first, with tool calls collapsed\n- [ ] Output is capped (runes, default 8,000); past the cap the reader only counts lines, and the output says \"N more transcript records not shown\"\n- [ ] `aside add`, Cursor, Codex and missing-file jots print `transcript: unavailable`, each with its own reason (Codex: \"Codex transcripts aren't read yet\", even when a path is stored)\n- [ ] `promote --with-reply` and `activity` treat Codex jots as having no readable transcript (moved from #83)\n- [ ] Tests use inline JSONL records in a temp file, like the existing reply-reader tests\n- [ ] `aside` usage text lists the new subcommand\n- [ ] Hand test after merge, read-only against the real database (AGENTS.md): `aside activity 31` (a 6.8 MB Desktop transcript, about 927 prompt and reply records after the jot) finishes quickly, stays within the cap and says how many records it left out\n- [ ] Any README or `docs/reference.md` example of `activity` is real output and names the version it was checked on (AGENTS.md)\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-14T00:09:51Z",
    "labels": [
     {
      "name": "ready-for-agent"
     }
    ]
   },
