    "title": "Codex hook stores transcript_path",
    "state": "closed",
    "body": "Implements: D3 — docs/proposals/jot-status-check.md\nBlocked by: None (can start immediately)\nParent: #78\n\n## What to build\n\nNew Codex jots save the transcript path from the Codex hook payload in their metadata, the same way Claude jots do. Nothing reads it yet: `activity` still answers \"unavailable\" for Codex in v1, and `promote --with-reply` keeps reading Claude transcripts only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A Codex hook payload with `transcript_path` stores it in the jot's metadata\n- [ ] A payload with a null or missing `transcript_path` stores nothing for it, as today\n- [ ] `promote --with-reply` still treats Codex jots as having no readable transcript (the `activity` half is in #82)\n- [ ] Hook tests cover the stored and absent cases\n- [ ] Hand test after merge (AGENTS.md): a Codex hook payload into a throwaway database stores the path\n",
