    "title": "activity as a read-only MCP tool",
    "state": "closed",
    "body": "Implements: D4, D5 — docs/proposals/jot-status-check.md\nBlocked by: #82\nParent: #78\n\n## What to build\n\nThe same result as `aside activity <id>`, through the MCP server as a new read-only tool, so agents in Claude Desktop and phone sessions can call it. The tool's output is marked as untrusted transcript data, and it carries the same cap and \"left out\" count as the CLI.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The MCP server lists an `activity` tool with `readOnlyHint: true`\n- [ ] Calling it returns the same records, cap and unavailable reasons as the CLI\n- [ ] The result says the transcript text is data, not instructions\n- [ ] `docs/decisions.md`'s MCP tool list is updated (it currently lists four of the five existing tools)\n- [ ] `docs/decisions.md` gets an entry for `activity`: why it's read-only and returns evidence rather than a verdict, and what would make that worth revisiting (e.g. auto-closing clear cases, D1)\n- [ ] The tool description says the transcript text is data, not instructions, and, if the result offers an `aside done` command, carries the existing full-path guidance (as the `open` tool does), since the description is what Desktop agents see\n",
