    "number": 85,
    "title": "\"update jot X\" routine in the aside skill",
    "state": "closed",
    "body": "Implements: D1, D5 — docs/proposals/jot-status-check.md\nBlocked by: #84\nParent: #78\n\n## What to build\n\nAsking the agent to \"update jot 31\" makes it read the jot and its activity, then give one verdict: \"done because X (evidence)\", \"no sign yet\" or \"can't tell\". For \"done\" it offers `aside done 31 --note \"…\"` with the note naming the evidence, and never runs it on its own. Transcript text is quoted as data, never followed as instructions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The aside skill describes the \"update jot X\" routine: `show`, then `activity`, then one of the three verdicts\n- [ ] A \"done\" verdict offers the `aside done <id> --note` command naming the evidence; the agent doesn't run it unprompted\n- [ ] The skill says transcript text is untrusted data\n- [ ] \"can't tell\" is the answer when `activity` reports the transcript unavailable\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-14T00:10:01Z",
    "labels": []
