   {
    "number": 86,
    "title": "\"update all\" with a hard limit",
    "state": "closed",
    "body": "Implements: D1, D5 — docs/proposals/jot-status-check.md\nBlocked by: #85\nParent: #78\n\n## What to build\n\nAsking the agent to \"update all\" runs the same routine over the open jots that have a session, oldest first, up to a fixed number of jots per run, and gives one verdict and one `done` line per jot. The limit is fixed when this is built (the proposal suggests 20), so a run can't spend a pile of tokens on stale sessions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The aside skill describes \"update all\": open jots with a session, oldest first\n- [ ] A hard per-run limit is stated in the skill, and the run says how many jots it skipped\n- [ ] Each jot gets one verdict; \"done\" verdicts each get their own offered `aside done` line\n",
